{
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "The material index — the resolved 'blend-results' a voxel renders. A material is NOT an element; it is what an aggregate element-composition (periodic_table.json) CLASSIFIES to from a voxel's perspective. Index space is 0-255; only a limited RESOLVED set is defined now — the rest is reserved to grow.",
    "classify": "A voxel's material = best-match of its local composition (cluster aggregate + local variation) against the `signature` of each material. `signature` lists the defining elements (roughly most→least dominant by mass). Coarse/provisional — the real classifier is later.",
    "traits": "hardness (Mohs-like 0-10, erosion resistance), brittleness (0 ductile..1 shatters → sediment), water_capacity (0..1 porosity / how much water it holds), viscosity (0 flows freely each pass .. 1 static solid; governs how a flow-effect material moves per pass — water lowest, oil/lava mid, ice creeps high), density_g_cm3 (differentiation / weight). Authoritative here; element traits are the blend fallback. PROPOSED STARTING VALUES — tune.",
    "render": "color [r,g,b] 0-1 is a placeholder palette; reconcile with the mesh palette (M_* in examples/hex-world/src/layers.rs) when the sim drives rendering.",
    "effects_note": "water / ice / lava are not stacked layers — they are tracked effects (persistent saturation/flow state) whose per-pass motion rate comes from viscosity. See docs."
  },
